.TH PACMANBAR 1 "2026-09-20" "caveutils" "caveutils Manual"
.SH NAME
pacmanbar \- a podman/pacman-style transfer bar for shell scripts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacmanbar
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pacmanbar
.nf

  pacmanbar                       run a short demo (no args)
  pacmanbar <cur> <total> [label]        draw one frame (\\r, to stderr)
  pacmanbar watch <file> <total> [label] poll <file>'s size until it
                                         reaches <total>, drawing as it grows

Sizes in bytes. `watch` also shows a live transfer rate and returns 0 when
the file reaches <total>, or 1 if it stops growing for ~10 s. Width adapts
to $COLUMNS / `tput cols`. Nothing is printed to stdout - safe to wrap.
.fi
